Cloud ACLI transport from re-running `jira workitem create` after a non-zero exit, because the create may already have landed. The code review of that change named 2 sibling paths with the same shape; neither is changed there:\n- Data Center: `_IssuesMixin.create_issue` (`src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py`) wraps the REST create in `_with_connection_retry`, which re-runs it on connection faults, including a fault after the request was sent.\n- Cloud comments: `_NON_REPLAYABLE_COMMANDS` in `src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_subprocess.py` lists only `jira workitem create`, so `jira workitem comment create` is still retried after any non-zero exit and can post a duplicate comment.\n\nNot established: whether either path has produced a duplicate in production. That needs a search of the Jira project for duplicate issues created seconds apart, and for repeated comments.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each of the 2 paths either no longer replays a write that may have landed (verified by a regression test that fails the first attempt after the write is recorded and asserts one result), or is shown with evidence to be safe.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["bridge"],"ticket_id":"0e48-b2df-17eb-407d","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Jira writes that create something are still replayed after an ambiguous failure: DC create on connection faults, ACLI comment create","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["5228df5c-f317-4128-aa1e-798cc22bdb15","66361f40-e117-47a1-8405-f7fed578d436"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795095413804438109,"uuid":"e76730c4-4230-4e6c-89d6-1185395aeb37"